# Build context exclusions for deploy/Dockerfile.
#
# The correctness entry is dist/. Without it a developer's stale local dist/
# rides into the build context: the backend stage's `COPY . .` lands it in
# /build/dist, and mage only adds gpx_* binaries alongside whatever is already
# there. The runtime stage then copies the frontend dist/ first and the backend
# dist/ second, so the stale plugin.json overwrites the one webpack just built
# and the image reports an old version -- with no error or warning anywhere.
#
# CI is unaffected because it builds from a clean checkout that has no dist/,
# which is exactly why this went unnoticed: only local builds were wrong.
#
# .git/ is deliberately NOT excluded. Go stamps VCS information into the binary
# from it, and dropping it would silently change what `go version -m` reports on
# the shipped binary.

# The correctness fix.
dist/

# Large or irrelevant; excluded only so the context stays small.
node_modules/
.playwright-mcp/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
coverage/
artifacts/
work/
ci/
pkg-root/
*.zip
*.sha1
.env
docs/internal/
